# DocSense — Local Environment Variables
# DO NOT commit the real .env file to GitHub. It is already excluded via .gitignore.
# Never paste real key values into chat, screenshots, or commit messages.
#
# Copy this file to .env and fill in the values you have. Every variable
# below is left deliberately EMPTY — nothing here is a working default.
#
# VARIABLE NAMES ARE CASE-SENSITIVE and must be copied exactly as written
# (RAG_Gemini, not RAG_GEMINI). Windows environment variables happen to be
# case-insensitive, so a wrong case can appear to work locally and then
# break on Linux/macOS.


# =====================================================================
# 1. ANSWER PROVIDERS — generation (Stage 6) + grading (Stage 7)
# =====================================================================
# These 7 keys drive the multi-provider rotation in
# generation/provider_rotation.py. See TDR.md Section 2i for the full
# reasoning; the short version is that Gemini's sibling Flash-tier models
# share capacity and failed together, leaving 5 of 11 Stage 7 questions
# unmeasured, so answer calls now rotate across INDEPENDENT vendors.
#
# All 7 are OpenAI-compatible (Cohere via /compatibility/v1, Gemini via
# /v1beta/openai), so one HTTP path serves all of them.
#
# Rotation is STICKY: one provider serves every question until it fails,
# then the next provider re-answers that same question from scratch.
# You do NOT need all 7 filled — one working key is enough to run.
#
# Status as verified 2026-10-26 (see TDR 2i for the full table):
#   RAG_Groq       working, fastest, citations accepted
#   RAG_NVIDIA     working, citations accepted
#   RAG_Cohere     working; trial keys are NON-COMMERCIAL, 1,000 calls/month
#   RAG_OpenRouter working; free models ~20 req/min and ~50 req/day
#   RAG_Gemini     unreliable at test time (1 success in 5 attempts)
#   RAG_SiliconFlow      disabled in code — signup credit exhausted (HTTP 402)
#   RAG_OpenCode_Console disabled in code — free tier is gated to the
#                        OpenCode app itself (403) and paid models need
#                        funds (402)
#
# To re-enable either disabled provider after adding credit, set
# enabled=True on its entry in generation/provider_rotation.py PROVIDERS.
#
# Context windows for the pinned models, and Groq's and NVIDIA's current
# free-tier quotas, could NOT be verified from official documentation —
# treat them as unknown rather than assuming a value.

RAG_Gemini=
RAG_Groq=
RAG_NVIDIA=
RAG_OpenRouter=
RAG_SiliconFlow=
RAG_Cohere=
RAG_OpenCode_Console=


# =====================================================================
# 2. GOOGLE GEMINI KEYS — embeddings (Stage 4) + image reading (Stage 3) ONLY
# =====================================================================
# These are NO LONGER used for answer generation or grading. Since the
# Section 2i change they serve exactly two purposes:
#   - Stage 4: query and chunk embeddings (gemini-embedding-001 @ 768 dims)
#   - Stage 3: reading charts/diagrams/tables out of document images
#              (GEMINI_VISION_MODEL, default gemini-3.6-flash)
#
# Each key MUST belong to a DIFFERENT Google Cloud project: Gemini's
# free-tier limits are applied per project, not per key or per account,
# so multiple keys from the SAME project do not increase your quota.
# See TDR.md Section 2d for the full documented reasoning.
#
# You do not need all 7 slots filled — GEMINI_API_KEY alone is enough to
# get started. The extra keys only give the rotation more quota to fall
# back on when one is exhausted.
#
# NOTE ON QUOTAS: an earlier version of this file quoted a specific
# per-day request figure for the generation model. That number applied to
# gemini-2.5-flash, which is no longer available to new API keys at all
# (confirmed 2026-10-26: it now returns a 404 "no longer available to new
# users"). Per-model free-tier limits change without notice, so no figure
# is quoted here — check ai.google.dev/gemini-api/docs/rate-limits for the
# current embedding and vision limits instead of trusting a hardcoded one.
#
# RETRIEVAL DEPENDS ON THESE KEYS. Every query needs one embedding call,
# so if this pool is exhausted, retrieval fails even when several answer
# providers are healthy. This is the largest remaining single-vendor risk
# in the system (TDR 2i, known limitation 2).

GEMINI_API_KEY=
GEMINI_API_KEY_2=
GEMINI_API_KEY_3=
GEMINI_API_KEY_4=
GEMINI_API_KEY_5=
GEMINI_API_KEY_6=
GEMINI_API_KEY_7=

# Optional override for the Stage 3 vision model.
# GEMINI_VISION_MODEL=

# Optional: set to "local" to use the opt-in local BGE embedding backend
# instead of Gemini. Requires recreating the Qdrant collection at the
# local model's own dimensionality — see TDR.md Section 2h before using.
# DOCSENSE_EMBEDDING_BACKEND=


# =====================================================================
# 3. OPTIONAL / NOT CURRENTLY USED
# =====================================================================
# --- Anthropic Claude (only if billing is set up later; see TDR 2a) ---
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# --- Voyage AI embeddings (only if switching back from Gemini; see TDR 2a) ---
# VOYAGE_API_KEY=

# --- Qdrant (only for a hosted/cloud instance instead of local embedded mode) ---
# QDRANT_URL=
# QDRANT_API_KEY=
